<h1 class="page-title">Post <nxl expr="id" /></h1>
<p class="lede">
  The <code>:id</code> in the route path is bound as <code>id</code> before this
  page runs, so it is used without any plumbing.
</p>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>The values that were bound</h2>
  <p>Path parameter <code>id</code>: <code><nxl expr="id" /></code></p>
  <p>Query string <code>q</code>: <code><nxl expr='q' /></code></p>
  <p>Request path <code>path</code>: <code><nxl expr='path' /></code></p>
  <p>Method <code>method</code>: <code><nxl expr='method' /></code></p>
</section>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>Try another</h2>
  <ul class="list">
    <li><a href="/posts/42">/posts/42</a></li>
    <li><a href="/posts/hello-world">/posts/hello-world</a></li>
    <li><a href="/posts/7?q=from+the+query+string">/posts/7?q=from...</a></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>Escaping a path parameter</h2>
  <p>
    A path segment arrives raw and is escaped when printed, so a segment
    containing a tag is shown as text instead of becoming one.
  </p>
</section>